window.products.push({"id":1162835,"name":"Babish Blue Steel Fry Pan, 12-inch","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":50.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/614SpmmK4dL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"When dinner prep hits crunchtime, you need the G.O.A.T to get the job done. The Babish 12-inch Blue Steel Frying Pan scores high in delivering exceptional texture and flavors. Its high-quality blue steel construction heats up rapidly and evenly, perfect for sautéing, stir-frying, or any cooking style. Over time, carbon steel forms a protective rust-resistant layer that is naturally nonstick! It comes with a double-riveted stainless steel handle for a sure grip when tossing and frying. Safe to use on the grill and on gas, electric, ceramic, glass and induction stoves. Oven safe up to 500°F. Handwash only.HOW TO SEASON CARBON STEEL - STOVE METHOD:- Wash pan with warm soapy water dry with towel and then place on stovetop and heat to ensure the pan is thoroughly dried.- Once pan is dry use oil of choice and with a paper towel apply around the interior and exterior of the pan. You may also continue to rub the pan with a hand towel to ensure the oil is evenly coated throughout the pan.- Place you pan back on the stove and heat until smoking. Be sure to also heat the sides of the pan over the flame to ensure the entire surface area is heated.- Once smoking turn the heat off and allow the pan to cool quickly. HOW TO SEASON CARBON STEEL - OVEN METHOD:- Place a foil lined baking sheet into the bottom rack of your oven.- Preheat your oven to 475F to 500F.-While oven is preheating - Wash pan with warm soapy water dry with towel and then place on stovetop and heat to ensure the pan is thoroughly dried.- One pan is dry use oil of choice and with a paper towel apply around the interior and exterior of the pan. You may also continue to rub the pan with a hand towel to ensure the oil is evenly coated throughout the pan.- Place pan into the fully heated oven upside down on the rack above the foil lined baking sheet.- Leave pan in the oven for an hour. After an hour turn off the oven but leave the pan in there until it is cool to the touch.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/614SpmmK4dL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Babish","source_asin":"B09HWRXF8H","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-1162835","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09HWRXF8H","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B09HWRXF8H","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
